From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:30:00 +0000
Subject: arm64: dts: allwinner: h616: Make the GPU a cooling device and
 throttle it from the GPU thermal zone

The gpu-thermal zone only has the 110 degC critical trip and the GPU
node cannot act as a cooling device, so once a board describes GPU OPPs
(panfrost devfreq, 306-600 MHz on the H616) the only reaction to a hot
Mali-G31 is a shutdown.

Add #cooling-cells to the GPU node and a passive "gpu-alert" trip at
85 degC (2 degC hysteresis) mapped to the GPU with THERMAL_NO_LIMIT, so
step_wise lowers the GPU OPP first. 85 degC is the same level as the
H616 CPU alert trip and the GPU alert mainline uses on the H6 (same
Mali/THS generation; the vendor BSP for sun50iw9 throttles the GPU from
its 90 degC CPU target trip). The passive trip has no effect on boards
without a GPU OPP table, because panfrost then registers no devfreq
cooling device and the map stays unbound.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h616.dtsi
@@ -248,6 +248,7 @@
 			clock-names = "core", "bus";
 			power-domains = <&prcm_ppu 2>;
 			resets = <&ccu RST_BUS_GPU>;
+			#cooling-cells = <2>;
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
@@ -1863,10 +1864,23 @@
 			sustainable-power = <1100>;
 
 			trips {
-				gpu_temp_critical: gpu-trip-0 {
+				gpu_alert: gpu-alert {
+					temperature = <85000>;
+					hysteresis = <2000>;
+					type = "passive";
+				};
+
+				gpu_temp_critical: gpu-crit {
 					temperature = <110000>;
-					type = "critical";
 					hysteresis = <0>;
+					type = "critical";
+				};
+			};
+
+			cooling-maps {
+				map0 {
+					trip = <&gpu_alert>;
+					cooling-device = <&gpu THERMAL_NO_LIMIT THERMAL_NO_LIMIT>;
 				};
 			};
 		};
